 array arr of integers and a positive integer k, return a sorted list \n    of length k with the maximum k numbers in arr.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Define constants for input validation as per specification.\n    MIN_ARRAY_LENGTH = 1\n    MAX_ARRAY_LENGTH = 1000\n    MIN_ARRAY_ELEMENT = -1000\n    MAX_ARRAY_ELEMENT = 1000\n\n    # Input validation, raising ValueError for invalid inputs as per design.\n    if not isinstance(arr, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'arr' must be a list.\")\n    if not all(isinstance(x, int) for x in arr):\n        raise ValueError(\"All elements in 'arr' must be integers.\")\n    \n    arr_len = len(arr)\n    if not (MIN_ARRAY_LENGTH <= arr_len <= MAX_ARRAY_LENGTH):\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"Length of 'arr' must be between {MIN_ARRAY_LENGTH} and {MAX_ARRAY_LENGTH} (inclusive).\"\n        )\n    if not all(MIN_ARRAY_ELEMENT <= x <= MAX_ARRAY_ELEMENT for x in arr):\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"Elements in 'arr' must be between {MIN_ARRAY_ELEMENT} and {MAX_ARRAY_ELEMENT} (inclusive).\"\n        )\n    if not isinstance(k, int) or k < 0 or k > arr_len:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"Input 'k' must be a non-negative integer and less than or equal to len(arr) ({arr_len}).\"\n        )\n\n    if k == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Use a min-heap to efficiently find the k largest elements.\n    min_heap = []\n    for num in arr:\n        if len(min_heap) < k:\n            heapq.heappush(min_heap, num)\n        elif num > min_heap[0]:\n            heapq.heapreplace(min_heap, num)\n    \n    # Sort the k elements from the heap in ascending order before returning.\n    return sorted(min_heap)", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/122": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/122", "solution": "def add_elements(arr: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of elements with at most two digits from the first `k` elements of `arr`.\n 